5. FORKS AND DERIVATIVE PROJECTS
============================================================

Forks and other non-commercial Derivative Projects are
permitted.

A Fork must:

(a) clearly identify itself as a derivative of LumaOS;

(b) provide a visible reference to the Original Project;

(c) provide a link to the official LumaOS project whenever
    reasonably possible;

(d) retain this License and all applicable copyright notices;

(e) clearly distinguish itself from the Original Project;

(f) use a name that does not imply that the Fork is the
official LumaOS project;

(g) not use the official LumaOS logo or other official branding;

(h) not represent itself as being developed, maintained,
    endorsed, or officially supported by the LumaOS project;

(i) remain non-commercial.

A Fork may be substantially modified and may evolve into an
independent operating system or software project, provided that
the requirements of this License continue to be respected for
the portions derived from LumaOS.

